From dd837772d6e2e3e92ac87b59a2f19ba07db0dde2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Paunovic <royalnet026@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:04:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: npu: rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core: allow
 operating-points-v2

The NPU cores are pinned to a fixed assigned-clock-rate today, but the
hardware supports the same frequency range the GPU does, and the SoC
exposes the clock through SCMI and the supply through a regulator the
binding already requires.

Allow a core to reference an OPP table so DVFS can be described in DT
rather than hardcoded.  The property is optional: the three cores share
one clock and one supply, so scaling is driven from the core that owns
them and only that core needs a table.

Signed-off-by: Igor Paunovic <royalnet026@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/npu/rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.yaml      | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/npu/rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/npu/rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.yaml
index 7350b5121..5653386d2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/npu/rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/npu/rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.yaml
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@ properties:
 
   npu-supply: true
 
+  operating-points-v2: true
+
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
-- 
2.53.0

